- How would you handle retroactive policy changes for historical data?

Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a scalable OTCA path with privacy-first constraints, multi-region residency, dynamic redaction, and compliant purge workflows.

Key Concepts
- Per-tenant residency and data locality
- Dynamic, versioned redaction rules
- Immutable regional logs and global canonical events
- Canary rollouts and zero-downtime config reloads
- GDPR/CCPA purge and auditability

Code Example
```javascript
function redact(event, policy) {
  const out = { ...event };
  if (policy.redactPII && out.user?.email) delete out.user.email;
  if (policy.redactPhone && out.user?.phone) delete out.user.phone;
  return out;
}
```

Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate purge requests across regions with clock skew?
- Which metrics indicate redaction misfires under load and how would you triage them?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design offline-capable telemetry at the edge with guaranteed delivery and strict tenancy isolation.

## Key Concepts

- Edge buffering, per-tenant isolation, idempotent writes
- Out-of-order handling and replay-safe semantics
- Pluggable sinks and backpressure-aware flushing
- Testing offline durability and cross-tenant isolation

## Code Example

```javascript
class EdgeBuffer {
  constructor() { this.store = new Map(); }
  add(event) {
    const key = `${event.tenant_id}:${event.seq}`;
    this.store.set(key, event);
  }
  flush(toSink) { /* dedupe by (tenant_id, seq) and send in order */ }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you implement exactly-once semantics across edge and cloud sinks?
- How do you test failure modes like prolonged offline periods and partial flushes?

